## Project Overview

**hppx** is a zero-dependency HTTP Parameter Pollution (HPP) protection middleware for Node.js/Express, written in TypeScript. It sanitizes `req.query`, `req.body`, and `req.params` by detecting and reducing duplicate/array parameters, blocking prototype pollution keys, and supporting flexible whitelisting with multiple merge strategies.

- **Package name:** `hppx`
- **Current version:** `0.2.8`
- **License:** MIT
- **Author:** Hiprax
- **Repository:** [GitHub](https://github.com/Hiprax/hppx)
- **NPM:** [NPM](https://www.npmjs.com/package/hppx)
- **Node.js requirement:** >= 18
- **Runtime dependencies:** None (zero production dependencies)

---

## Architecture

### Single-Source Module

The entire middleware is implemented in a single file: `src/index.ts` (~1006 lines). There is no complex module hierarchy. The file exports:

- **Default export:** `hppx()` — the Express middleware factory
- **Named exports:** `sanitize()`, `DANGEROUS_KEYS`, `DEFAULT_STRATEGY`, `DEFAULT_SOURCES`, `__resetPathSegmentCache()`
- **Type exports:** `RequestSource`, `MergeStrategy`, `SanitizeOptions`, `HppxOptions`, `SanitizedResult`

> **Note on `__resetPathSegmentCache`:** This function is a test-only helper (annotated `@internal`) that clears the module-level path-segment parse cache. It leaks into the public `.d.ts` as a side-effect of the single-file architecture. Consumers must not depend on it — it exists solely so tests can verify cache-eviction behavior without exposing the internal `Map`.

### Dual-Format Build

The project builds to both ESM (`.mjs`) and CommonJS (`.cjs`) using `tsup`. A custom esbuild footer in `tsup.config.ts` merges the default and named exports for CommonJS so `require("hppx")` works without `.default`. tsup auto-generates both `dist/index.d.ts` (ESM) and `dist/index.d.cts` (CJS) from `src/index.ts`; the two files are kept in symbol-parity by `scripts/check-dts-parity.mjs`, which runs as part of `npm run prepare`.

### Express Request Augmentation

`src/index.ts` itself contains a top-level `declare module "express-serve-static-core"` block that augments the Express `Request` interface with optional `queryPolluted`, `bodyPolluted`, and `paramsPolluted` properties (all `Record<string, unknown>`). Keeping the augmentation inline ensures tsup emits it into both `dist/index.d.ts` and `dist/index.d.cts`. A compile-time smoke test in `tests/types/express-augment.test-d.ts` verifies the augmentation reaches consumers under `npm run typecheck`.

