## Testing

### Framework

- **Jest** with **ts-jest** transform
- **supertest** for HTTP integration testing
- **Test environment:** Node.js

### Test Files Overview

| File                                | Focus                   | Key Tests                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |
| ----------------------------------- | ----------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `hppx.test.ts`                      | Core functionality      | Query/body handling, merge strategies, nested whitelists, multi-middleware                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  |
| `hppx.security.test.ts`             | Security                | Array limits, key length, prototype pollution, null bytes, options validation (incl. logger/onPollutionDetected), error handling, onPollutionDetected callback, pollution logging, circular reference protection, depth limits in expandObjectPaths/safeDeepClone                                                           |
| `hppx.coverage.test.ts`             | Edge cases              | setReqPropertySafe edge cases, mergeValues validation, leaf matching, logger failures, null-prototype objects, frozen properties, safeDeepClone depth/circular ref/key filtering, setIn dangerous last-key, processNode undefined handling, non-Error throw wrapping, content-type absence, whitelist cache hit              |
| `hppx.edgecases.test.ts`            | Boundary conditions     | Bracket notation expansion, checkBodyContentType=none, trimValues, malformed keys, whitelist prefix subtree, non-plain-object parts, combine strategy flattening, preserveNull: false behavior, sanitize() options validation                                                                                               |
| `hppx.more.test.ts`                 | Extended features       | Strict mode, excludePaths, content type handling, maxDepth/maxKeys limits, dangerous key stripping, sanitize() standalone usage                                                                                                                                                                                             |
| `hppx.performance.test.ts`          | Performance             | Path caching, large object handling, whitelist helper performance, memory efficiency, cache size limits, maxArrayLength truncation precision                                                                                                                                                                                 |
| `hppx.express5.test.ts`             | Express 5 integration   | Lazy `req.query` getter, `Object.defineProperty` shadowing, frozen property warning, defineProperty failure fallback                                                                                                                                                                                                        |
| `hppx.edgeruntime.test.ts`          | Edge runtime            | `process` undefined fallback, logger failure fallback to `console.warn`/`console.error`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    |
| `hppx.whitelist-semantics.test.ts`  | Semantics / pins        | `req.params` e2e (reduction + paramsPolluted + strict), empty-array `{x:[]}` behavior, scalar↔dotted key collision (both orders), `combine`+`whitelist` raw-array preservation, `maxArrayLength` truncation exact values, `strict`+`whitelist` 400 behavior, three-signal semantics (full/partial whitelist), cross-source partial mutation on limit throw |
| `types/express-augment.test-d.ts`   | Type-only smoke test    | Compile-time assertion that `queryPolluted`, `bodyPolluted`, `paramsPolluted` are visible on `express.Request` at consumer sites                                                                                                                                                                                            |

### Test Conventions

- Tests disable pollution logging by default (`logPollution: false`) for clean output
- Integration tests use `supertest` with Express apps built inline
- `buildApp()` or `appWith()` helper functions create test Express apps
- Coverage target: 95%+ on all metrics (203 tests across 9 suites, 99.72% stmts, 95.01% branches, 100% funcs, 100% lines)

### Running Tests

```bash
npm test              # Run all tests
npm run test:coverage # Run with coverage report
npm run test:watch    # Watch mode
```

