## Commands Reference

```bash
# Build / test / lint
npm run build            # Build with tsup (ESM + CJS)
npm run clean            # Remove dist/ directory
npm run dev              # Watch mode build
npm test                 # Run Jest tests
npm run test:coverage    # Tests with coverage
npm run test:watch       # Tests in watch mode
npm run typecheck        # TypeScript type checking (tsc --noEmit)
npm run lint             # ESLint validation
npm run format           # Prettier formatting (writes)
npm run format:check     # Prettier formatting check (no writes)
npm run check-dts        # DTS symbol parity (.d.ts vs .d.cts)
npm run check-types-pack # arethetypeswrong validation on packed tarball
npm run prepare          # Pre-publish build (runs automatically on npm publish)
npm run verify           # Run every quality gate locally (mirrors CI)

# Release flow
npm run branch -- feat my-thing  # Create conventional branch from latest main
npm run sync                     # Pull main, prune deleted-remote local branches
npm run release:prepare -- patch # Bump + branch + commit + push (opens PR)
npm run release:tag              # Tag current main, push (triggers release.yml)
```

## CI / Release Infrastructure

- **`.github/workflows/ci.yml`** — On push to main and on every PR. Matrix
  Node 18 / 20 / 22 / 24 on ubuntu-latest: `build`, `check-dts`,
  `check-types-pack`, `typecheck`, `lint`, `format:check`,
  `test -- --coverage`. Codecov upload runs only on the Node 22 leg.
- **`.github/workflows/release.yml`** — On `v*.*.*` tag push (or
  `workflow_dispatch`). Re-runs every gate, verifies `package.json` version
  matches the tag, then `npm publish --provenance --access public` via OIDC,
  then creates a GitHub Release. The release body is extracted from
  `CHANGELOG.md` via awk; the extractor matches the project's
  `## vX.Y.Z — Title (YYYY-MM-DD)` heading style (em dash, not bracket).
- **`.github/workflows/codeql.yml`** — `security-and-quality` query suite on
  push, PR, and weekly schedule.
- **Required GitHub secrets:**
  - `NPM_TOKEN` — **Automation** token from npmjs.com → Access Tokens. Used by
    `release.yml`. Bypasses 2FA prompts on write while leaving the account's
    "Authorization and writes" 2FA enabled for everything else.
  - `CODECOV_TOKEN` — Repository Upload Token from codecov.io after installing
    the Codecov GitHub App on the repo.
- **CHANGELOG heading convention:** `## vX.Y.Z — <Title> (<YYYY-MM-DD>)`.
  The release workflow's awk extractor depends on this shape; do not
  switch to `## [X.Y.Z] - YYYY-MM-DD` (the npm-bootstrap default) without
  also updating `release.yml` and `scripts/release-tag.mjs`.

## Repo-Side Hardening (configured on GitHub, not in this tree)

Applied via the GitHub API; not visible in source code. Listed here so
future sessions don't accidentally undo them.

- **Branch ruleset on `main`** (id 16288916): blocks `deletion`,
  `non_fast_forward`; requires 5 status checks (`Test on Node 18.x`,
  `20.x`, `22.x`, `24.x`, `Analyze (javascript-typescript)`); requires
  linear history; `current_user_can_bypass: never`.
- **Tag ruleset on `refs/tags/v[0-9]*`** (id 16297738, name
  `release tags`): blocks `deletion`, `non_fast_forward`, `update` —
  published version tags are immutable, even for the owner.
- **Security features enabled:** secret scanning, secret scanning push
  protection, Dependabot alerts, Dependabot security updates, private
  vulnerability reporting.
- **Merge settings:** squash + rebase only (`allow_merge_commit: false`),
  auto-merge enabled, `delete_branch_on_merge: true`, squash commit
  uses PR title + body.

**Implication for the release flow:** direct pushes to `main` are
blocked by the branch ruleset. Use the PR-based flow (`npm run
release:prepare -- <bump>` → merge PR → `npm run release:tag`). Tag
creation is allowed but tag deletion/movement is not — never try to
"retag" a published version; if you need to fix a release, ship a new
patch version instead.

