## Code Style & Conventions

### Formatting (Prettier)

- Print width: 100 characters
- Semicolons: enabled
- Single quotes: disabled (double quotes)
- Trailing commas: all

### Linting (ESLint)

- Flat config in `eslint.config.mjs` (ESLint 10 — legacy `.eslintrc.*` is no longer supported by ESLint anyway)
- Composes `js.configs.recommended` from `@eslint/js`, `tseslint.configs.recommended` and `tseslint.configs.stylistic` from `typescript-eslint`, and `eslint-config-prettier` (last, to disable conflicting stylistic rules)
- `@typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any`: off (deliberately, since Express types are loose)
- `@typescript-eslint/consistent-type-definitions`: `interface` enforced
- Ignores: `dist/**`, `node_modules/**`, `coverage/**`, generated `.d.ts`/`.d.cts`

### TypeScript Conventions

- Strict mode with `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`
- Interfaces preferred over type aliases for object shapes
- `any` used sparingly and deliberately for Express compatibility
- Non-null assertions (`!`) used on array indexing after bounds checks

### Naming Conventions

- Functions: camelCase (`sanitizeKey`, `buildWhitelistHelpers`)
- Types/Interfaces: PascalCase (`HppxOptions`, `SanitizedResult`)
- Constants: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE (`DANGEROUS_KEYS`, `DEFAULT_STRATEGY`)
- Internal flags: prefixed with `__hppx` (`__hppxProcessed_query`)

